<Order xmlns="urn:oasis:names:specification:ubl:schema:xsd:Order-2" xmlns:cac="urn:oasis:names:specification:ubl:schema:xsd:CommonAggregateComponents-2" xmlns:cbc="urn:oasis:names:specification:ubl:schema:xsd:CommonBasicComponents-2" xmlns:ext="urn:oasis:names:specification:ubl:schema:xsd:CommonExtensionComponents-2"><cbc:CustomizationID>urn:fdc:peppol.eu:poacc:trns:order:3</cbc:CustomizationID><cbc:ProfileID>urn:fdc:peppol.eu:poacc:bis:ordering:3</cbc:ProfileID><cbc:ID>S00701</cbc:ID><cbc:IssueDate>2026-03-31</cbc:IssueDate><cbc:OrderTypeCode>220</cbc:OrderTypeCode><cbc:Note>Purchase Terms and Conditions of Sale
Order. This order is made and entered into as of the order date, by and between FixturFab, Inc., a Delaware corporation (â€œFixturFabâ€), and customer.  Final Customer Design Files. Unless agreed upon in writing, the lead time and price for the applicable FixturFab Product (defined below) will increase if Customer Design Files are added or modified after the order date.Â In the event Customer Design Files are determined to be materially incomplete or inaccurate, necessitating redesign or rework, the customer will be responsible for associated time and materials costs to rectify the deficiencies.  Change Orders. Any customer change request(s) for any FixturFab Product, will require that the FixturFab and customer execute a mutually agreed upon Change Order before any additional work commences.Â   Payments. Undisputed invoices that are not paid within each invoiceâ€™s payment terms will be subject to a two percent (2%) monthly interest rate.  Delivery. All FixturFab Products shall be delivered FCA (defined below).  Payment Dispute. If customer intends to dispute any amount due under an invoice, customer must notify FixturFab in writing within ten business days prior to the invoiceâ€™s due date.  Limited Warranty. FixturFab warrants the FixturFab Products to be free from defects in workmanship and materials for one (1) year from the Shipping Date (â€œLimited Warrantyâ€). FixturFabâ€™s obligation and customerâ€™s exclusive remedy under this Limited Warranty is, at FixturFabâ€™s option, to either repair or replace the FixturFab Products, provided that customer returns the FixturFab Products to the location designated by FixturFab within the Limited Warranty period.  Limitation of Liability. IN NO EVENT WILL FIXTURFAB BE LIABLE FOR ANY CONSEQUENTIAL, INDIRECT, EXEMPLARY, SPECIAL, OR INCIDENTAL DAMAGES, EVEN IF FIXTURFAB HAS BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.Â   Publicity. Customer agrees that FixturFab may include customerâ€™s name and logo in a list of customers and also agrees that FixturFab may verbally reference the customer as a customer.  Customer Service Agreement. Customer understands and agrees that if the customer decides to purchase a Turnkey Test System, customer and FixturFab shall enter into a mutually agreed upon Customer Service Agreement for such Test System.  Definitions
Request For Quotation - The online form submitted by the customer to receive a FixturFab quotation. Customer Design Files - The technical files submitted by the customer in the Request For Quotation form. Change Order - An amendment that modifies the deliverables, price, or other terms in the original order. All Change Orders must be in writing and executed by the parties to the original order. FixturFab Products - means collectively Test Fixture, Test System, Test System Blueprint. Test Fixture - A hardware product with various tiers, such as a Development Test Fixture or Production Test Fixture. Test System Blueprint - A set of design files developed by FixturFab based on Customer Design Files. Test System - A Test Fixture that integrates electrical products developed by FixturFab or other commercial-off-the-shelf products. Turnkey Test System - A Test System that also integrates software products developed by FixturFab. FCA - Free Carrier is a standard trade term defined in the International Commercial Terms (Incoterms) by the International Chamber of Commerce. Customer Service Agreement - An agreement between FixturFab and the customer specifying detailed terms for orders containing more complex products, software, and recurring support.</cbc:Note><cbc:DocumentCurrencyCode>USD</cbc:DocumentCurrencyCode><cac:ValidityPeriod><cbc:EndDate>2026-05-29</cbc:EndDate></cac:ValidityPeriod><cac:OriginatorDocumentReference><cbc:ID>PO-FIXTURFAB-001</cbc:ID></cac:OriginatorDocumentReference><cac:BuyerCustomerParty><cac:Party><cac:PartyName><cbc:Name>AirGarage</cbc:Name></cac:PartyName><cac:PostalAddress><cbc:StreetName>2261 Market St # 4027</cbc:StreetName><cbc:CityName>San Francisco</cbc:CityName><cbc:PostalZone>94114-1612</cbc:PostalZone><cbc:CountrySubentity>California</cbc:CountrySubentity><cac:Country><cbc:IdentificationCode>US</cbc:IdentificationCode></cac:Country></cac:PostalAddress><cac:Contact><cbc:Name>AirGarage</cbc:Name></cac:Contact></cac:Party></cac:BuyerCustome